# The build context is the repository root — both images need packages/ and the design
# system, which live outside the app they belong to. Everything that cannot affect a
# build is excluded, because the context is uploaded to the daemon on every build.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state and secrets. `.env` in particular must never reach an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.local-storage
docker-compose.override.yml

# Nothing here is needed to build or run either service. `e2e/package.json` is the one
# exception: it is a workspace, so package-lock.json names it and `npm ci` fails if the
# manifest is missing — even though not a single test file is ever copied in.
e2e
!e2e/package.json
specs
infra
*.md
!README.md
